      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining OAuth Integration**\n\nI'm currently focused on the practical implementation, and I've decided to move forward with Google as the external OAuth provider. My immediate goal is to make sure the provider identifier is integrated into the code, and I'm currently figuring out the setup for a concrete implementation.\n\n\n**Implementing Google OAuth**\n\nI'm now writing the `start_oauth_login.py` file with Flask. I've defined the content, including Flask imports, the Google OAuth endpoint, and parameters. The priority is the redirect step for the authorization code flow, and I'll use the write tool to create the file. I will write the code for the web server and the redirect process. I'm focusing on simplicity for a clear demonstration.\n\n\n**Constructing Initial Login Script**\n\nI'm now outlining the structure for `start_oauth_login.py`.  It'll use Flask and placeholder credentials for Google OAuth. I'll define routes for initiating the login (redirecting to Google) and handling the redirect (which currently only prints the auth code). Next, I plan to create the file using the `write` tool.\n\n\n",
